scripts/fire.md:31:For a drain: `npx tsc --noEmit` + `npm run build` + the slice's own spec + affected adjacent suites + a boot probe (zero console/page errors, desktop + 390px). Full native runs — no splits needed. 🧮 **AND IF THE SLICE'S DIFF TOUCHES `src/sim/`, `src/systems/` OR `src/entities/`, THE BATTERY ALSO INCLUDES `npm run test:node-guards` (F-1460-1, second half of the cure; landed s1462 with the re-pin).** A slice-local spec is structurally incapable of seeing a **cross-cutting sim pin**, because the pin does not live in the slice's own suite — so a drain gated correctly and completely on the slice's specs can still move a number that another guard asserts, and nothing in the prescribed battery will say so. ⚠️ **That is not hypothetical, it is how F-1460-1 was born:** `4ab48743` (f1452-1 fort-solidity — gates the stuck-watchdog on `route.blocker` in `src/entities/Enemy.ts`, +139/-31 in `src/systems/BuildSystem.ts`) changed routing, therefore engagement, therefore **8 fewer kills over 20 waves**; it was deliberate and spec-green and reached main via drain `07213c73`, whose evidence reads *"4/4 own specs both projects"*. The Baron pin in `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` went stale that instant, `test:node-guards` went red **on every fire from 2026-08-04 to s1462**, and — the expensive part — **the red was wearing an excused class label (`cross-engine`), so for five fires nobody investigated it.** A red nobody investigates is worse than no test. 💡 **The general shape: a change is cross-cutting when it moves BEHAVIOUR the sim replays, not when it edits many files** — routing, blockers, targeting, spawn order and damage resolution all qualify while touching two files. Judge by the directory, not by the diff size; that is why this rule is keyed on paths a human cannot forget rather than on a judgement call. ⓘ **Cost, measured s1462 and stated honestly rather than waved at:** `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` is the battery's dominant term at **55.6 s** (its Baron test alone 8.5 s); the full battery is **284 tests / 281 pass / 3 skipped** and runs in one command. That is cheap against two days of a red board. 📈 **RE-MEASURED s1537 (F-1537-1) — every number in the previous sentence has drifted, and the DIRECTION is what matters: the battery is now `363 tests / 360 pass / 0 fail / 3 skipped` in `181.3 s`, and `gr-sim` alone is `12 tests / 79.9 s` (44% of the whole), its two Baron tests `15.0 s` + `14.2 s` where the old text says one at 8.5 s.** ⚠️ **Do not read the drift as rot in the pointer sense — the battery GREW on purpose (+79 tests since s1462) and the s1462 figures were honest when written; what is now false is only the CHEAPNESS ARGUMENT'S ARITHMETIC, so it is restated rather than deleted.** ⓘ Practical consequence for the fire that has to schedule it: **3 minutes serial, not one**, and a fire that overlaps it with a second battery will contaminate both (s1536 hung ~19 min doing exactly that on shared `claimed-spec-harness-guard`/`fixture-teardown` fixtures). **Run it ALONE.** It is still cheap against two days of a red board. ⚖️ **A failure here is a FINDING, never a re-pin reflex** — see the standing prohibition below and the comment at the pin site: re-pin only with a **named cause**, never to make a red go away (F-1441-3). **Merge-throughput tools (2026-07-06): (a) DISJOINT-PAIR BATCH — two lane drains may share ONE gate battery when their `git diff --name-only` sets vs their bases are disjoint (additive-only Balance.ts / vite-env.d.ts hunks excepted): merge both onto clean main, run one combined battery (both slices' specs + the union of adjacent suites), commit each path-scoped. On ANY failure revert both and fall back to strict serial. Never batch more than two; never batch when one touches files the other's spec exercises. (b) ⛔ **WITHDRAWN s1270 — this clause prescribed the exact thing §3.1 forbids.** It read: "the desktop and mobile playwright projects may run concurrently on two scratch ports when wall-time matters." Both of its premises are now measured false in the fire shell: concurrency is what MANUFACTURES the reds (17 drift reds / 18 at default workers vs 0 / 18 at `--workers=1`), and wall-time does not favour it anyway (**60.74 s concurrent vs 55.94 s serial**). Run the projects SERIALLY under `--workers=1`. The scratch-port family (5199/5231/5234) stays — that is Mistake #12 attribution hygiene and is unrelated. The gate CONTENT is never thinned — these optimize repetition, not rigor.** For lane drains: diff the worktree against ITS base commit (find it via the lane branch), classify LANE-TOUCHED vs MAIN-MOVED-ONLY per file, never blind-copy — 3-way graft when both moved. Merge onto CLEAN main only. Write `reviews/<slice>.md` (verdict, evidence, findings F-<id>, env exceptions with proof) + screenshots to `reviews/shots-<slice>/`. Findings that block: write a corrective task to tasks/queue/<slot>/ instead of merging. Art drains: QA raws vs the request's measured criteria, `node scripts/extract-alpha.mjs --key <hex> --grid CxR`, seam-law height checks, wire contracts, in-game screenshot review, LEDGER update.
