e this drain deletes (quoted in the review for retention; git keeps it at `80ace71c3`) shows `e2-hill-mine` and `e2-trestle` at **18 waves / 540000ms** (the cap) and `e2-incline` terminating at **wave 2 in ~80s** on both seeds. **Policy is untouched — the citation is F-E2S-3, the owner ruling naming all three BY NAME — and the error is the MASTER's, not the runner's**: it ordered the uniform phrasing, inheriting s1605's proof measured on `e2-hill-mine` alone. **(E) attended-owed, unchanged:** F-1653-3 · F-1650-1 · F-1649-1 · F-1639-3 (gates SEA-3) · F-1661-2 (write the AP-04 slice) · F-1661-4's two (BT-04's four forks as four numbers; the fairground engine slice). 💡 **THE LESSON, and it is the sibling of the last two fires':** s1660 found every instrument green while a ruling was silently reversed; s1661 found every instrument green while two pointed at already-refused work. **I found a red that was real, a red that was the machine's, and a firewall that was right about its subject and wrong about its scope — and only a control run could tell the first two apart.** A red is not evidence until you know whose it is. 🔺 **OWNER'S DESK — 21 awaiting a word (UNCHANGED; F-1662-1..3 add NOTHING — one is cured, one is fire-authorable, one is prose accuracy inside a ruling you already gave).** 🔺 **F-1659-1** · 🔺 **F-1657-3** · 🔺 **F-1656-3** · 🔺 **F-1653-2** · 🔺 **F-1648-1** · 🔺 **F-1640-1** · 🔺 **F-1637-2** · 🔺 **F-1625-4** · 🔺 **F-1617-1** · 🔺 **F-DOOR-6** · 🔺 **F-1608-2** · 🔺 **F-1193-3** · 🔺 **F-1501-3** · 🔺 **F-1601-1** · 🔺 **F-1510-1** · 🔺 **F-E2S-3** · 🔺 **F-1536-2** · 🔺 **F-1591-1** · 🔺 **F-1507-1** · 🔺 **F-E2S-4** · 🔺 **F-1101-1** — all 21 re-verified with `desk-state-audit --status` against the line-1 I inherited: **CLOSED=0 · OPEN=0 · BOTH=0 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=21 · UNRECORDED=0**, so none is a ghost and none should have been dropped. ⚖️ **Still the cheapest unblock on the board: F-1656-3** — three words (accept / retake at ≥460px raw / declare the rotation sheet lega