.5`, `'north'`, `null` **all** refuse — the last three being inputs the shipped test does not cover. 🔗 Traced the seam to prove the facing reaches a **real placed building** (`SeatedLockstepSim.ts:330` → `HeadlessContractSim.ts:642` → `BuildSystem.confirmPlacement`), which is why the master's FIREWALL LIFT went **unused and correctly so**. **GATES** (fire shell, `--workers=1`, detached worktree `gate-s1646` per §3.0b, merged+committed as ONE act per F-1589-5): tsc clean · build green · node-guards **ALONE** = **447 tests / 442 pass / 0 fail / 5 skip, ZERO `gr-sim` drift** · own suite **5 → 6, 6/6** · `same-game-audit` 3/3, **counts UNMOVED** (agent-lacks 439, equal 641) · `e2e/ap16-5-rotation-parity` **4/4** both projects · plain boot **2/2** desktop+390px, zero console/page errors. 📋 **(2) `f1643-2 SUITE-RED-INVENTORY REFRESH` AUTHORED + DISPATCHED to lane-a** (`3956a642b`, leaf registered same commit). **First fire at which its gate was open** — all four lanes `ahead=0` USABLE, this fire's drain fully committed before authoring; s1644 and s1645 each declined for want of exactly that. 🔬 **The harness was PROVED before the scope was written, because two facts neither BACKLOG row records would have sunk a guessed master:** `logs/suite-red-inventory-raw.json` **does not exist** (untracked, and the copy behind the 2026-07-28 snapshot is gone from disk — the reducer gives `ENOENT`, not a stale-but-working report), and **the command that produced that snapshot is documented nowhere**. Ran the whole pipeline on one cheap spec first; scope 1–2 is that proven sequence scaled up. ⚠️ **F-1646-3 — THE GATE'S LETTER IS NOT ITS PURPOSE, AND I ALMOST WALKED PAST THE DIFFERENCE.** The gate is written in terms of **lanes**; lanes are **not** the only load on this machine. With all four idle, `ps` showed **Blender at 100% CPU for 2h26m** (`-b …/landmark.blend`, a headless art-pipeline render) **plus `fseventsd` at 100%** — **2 of 16 physical cores saturated by work no lane instrument can see.** A fire checking only `lane-usable --all` would have called the box quiet and been wrong. That is exactly why the gate's third clause (*"state the concurrent load it ran under"*) exists, so the master obeys it literally at run start **and** end, and **scope 5 adds what no row asked for**: every failing spec file is re-run **serially once**, and anything that fails in parallel but passes serially is declared **load-attributable** rather than banked as an excused red — the precise outcome the RE-PRICED row calls *"strictly worse than the 13-day-old one it replaced."* 🧹 **(3) F-1646-2 — a GHOST LADDER ROW retired:** `ap16-5-build-rotation` sat `planned` while the work it names shipped **in full** under two leaves (`144b3291` + `57208ef8`); pointer WALKED, not assumed. ⓘ **`ghost-ladder-row-guard --strict` reports 0 here** — the leaf carries no `taskFile` and no BACKLOG row of its own, a shape outside its denominator — so this is filed as a finding, not cured by a second mechanism. 🏭 **BOARD: lane-a BUSY (f1643-2, just dispatched); lane-b (11 behind), lane-c (96), lane-d (56) IDLE + USABLE, all `ahead=0` clean; main + art queues empty.** 🚨 **READ BEFORE REFILLING:** lane-a is taking a **full-suite measurement**. Refilling b/c/d is lawful and I am not forbidding it — but **every lane you start becomes load inside that snapshot**, so either hold them until it lands, or refill and expect its scope-5 serial re-run to do more work. **Do not queue anything that edits `e2e/**` or `logs/suite-red-inventory*` until it drains.** **NEXT:** **(A)** 🔥 **AP-16-6 (the remaining verbs, classified)** — the last AP-16 rung, genuinely authorable: `StandingOrders.ts` is clear, the spec slice (`specs/agent-play/ap-16-same-game-law.md:35`) already classifies which of the nine tape-only actions are OWED vs EXEMPT with reasons. **Scope it to ONE verb per master** — five in one is not a slice. **(B)** **AP-03 (the Rider Protocol = `/skill.md`)** authorable; does not contend with (A)