propagation` · `citation-title` · `ghost-ladder-row --strict` · `nul-audit` · `status-archive-audit` (**0 permanently absent**) · `attended-owed` (1 open, attended-side only). 🔴 **AND IT EARNED ITS KEEP: `desk-declaration-guard` FAILED** — F-1646-1/2/3 had **no declaring BACKLOG row**, and F-1646-3 was buried *inside* the f1643-2 dispatch row, which is precisely the **F-1328-3 mention-inside-another-row** anti-pattern. Cured in `97be61408`; guard now **20/20 declared, PASS**. This is the F-1300-4 shape exactly: the battery a fire runs on the merged tree is structurally blind to the rows that fire is about to write. ⚠️ **STILL UNRUN, genuinely owed and NOT to be assumed green:** the fixture-spinning `.test.mjs` guards (`goal-tracker`, `stopped-leaf-supersession`, `stale-successor-pointer`, `block-class`, `claimed-spec-harness`, `desk-carryforward`, `desk-state-audit`, `stale-hold-verdict`, `banked-master-preflight`, `stale-ready-for-gates`) plus the three chained `bash` guards — all starved by the same contention. **I did NOT leave them merely unchecked:** I read `scripts/goal-tracker.test.mjs:61-101` and **replicated its schema assertions directly over all 783 leaves — 0 violations**, ids unique, `version 1`, 14 subgoals, every `merged` leaf carrying a 40-hex `mergeHash`, no `mergeCommit`; and verified my own leaf's `57208ef8…` **is ancestral to main** with its done receipt present. That is evidence about the *invariants*, not a substitute for the *guards* — **the next fire should re-run `npm run test:ledger-guards` on a quiet machine as its first act** and treat any red as possibly mine. 🚀 **DEPLOY OWED, NOT DONE — say so plainly rather than let a silent skip read as a skip-by-rule.** This fire merged gameplay code (`src/sim/SeatOrders.ts`), so the DEPLOY LAW applies and a bookkeeping-only exemption does **not**. `scripts/deploy.sh` was started, sat at **0% CPU for 20 minutes** at `tsc && vite build` — starved by the same 25-chromium contention — and was **stopped 