STATUS.md:96:- **s1644 handoff (line-1 archive):** Last updated: 2026-08-11T01:05Z s1644 handoff, lock CLEARED — 🔍 **A DRY FIRE THAT SPENT ITSELF ON ONE QUESTION AND CHANGED THE ANSWER. NO DRAIN EXISTED; lane-a HELD ap16-5 THE WHOLE TIME.** ✍️ **(1) AUTHORED + DISPATCHED — `f1643-1 FRONT-DOOR-PARITY REPAIR` IS QUEUED TO lane-b** (`tasks/lane-b-f1643-1-front-door-parity-repair.md`, leaf `f1643-1-front-door-parity-repair` registered in the SAME commit `50a02fd54`; master committed FIRST, lane-b refreshed SECOND — it was 61 behind, now at main — sequencing grep verified **1-in-lane** THIRD, pre-queue gate `--strict --queue` **CLEAR**, `cp` LAST: the F-1424-3 order). ⚠️ **IT DELIBERATELY REFUSES BOTH OPTIONS F-1643-1 OFFERED, AND MEASUREMENT IS THE ONLY REASON I KNEW TO.** The row asked to *"re-baseline the progression expectations … or retire the assertion"*. I opened the subject instead of inheriting the row, and all three findings changed the repair's shape. **(a) The attribution F-1643-1 marked INFERRED is now VERIFIED — by the cure's own comment:** `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs:46` (test `'gr-sim replays the same contract, seed, and orders byte-for-byte'`) reads *"AP-16-2: … the first-option pick moves from immediate to the trail deadline"*. **The sibling suite was re-pinned when the clock landed; this spec was not.** That IS the defect. **(b) The stdin test does not drift, it CRASHES — so no numeric re-baseline could ever have fixed it:** `scripts/gr-sim.mjs:99-101` is strict lockstep (one order batch per non-terminal turn), the clock adds turns, the spec's fixed **13-batch** stream runs out, and `scripts/gr-sim.mjs:179` throws `stdin ended while gr-sim was waiting for standing orders` → **rc=1, reproduced at 12, 20 and 30 batches.** ⭐ **(c) THE DOOR IS NOT BROKEN AND PARITY IS INTACT — which is the finding that matters, and the obvious repair would have buried it.** I built the reactive lockstep driver (one batch per view; `PICK_UPGRADE` on `now.pendingOffer[0].id`) and ran it twice byte-identical: **answered → `secured:true, waves:10, calls:26, defaultedPicks:0, eventLogHash:fnv1a32:fd705184`, first upgrade at level 2** — *exactly what the spec asserts today* — **vs silent → `secured:false, waves:8, defaultedPicks:6`, first upgrade at level 4.** ⚠️ **So pinning `waves:8`, the natural reading of "re-baseline", would have enshrined *"the agents' front door loses The Claim"* as normal. It is FALSE, and a green test would have defended it.** The spec is not stale about the OUTCOME; it is stale about **the CLIENT**, which never learned the verb AP-16-2 exists to add. 🔬 **Only the idle test is a genuine stale-value repair, and its cause is traced, not guessed:** `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:713` drives the clock every sim step and `:767-783` defaults only past `Balance.offers.pickSeconds` (20/30/10), so the idle hero — dead at **81.7 s** from late level-ups — never reaches a deadline, takes zero picks, is weaker, and dies a wave earlier. **Two drifted values, one cause, no bug.** The master also pins the `public/skill.md:78` silence promise (*"exactly like the browser clock"*), which **no test anywhere currently asserts**, and cuts the spec to `desktop-chrome` — it spawns `gr-sim.mjs` and never opens a page, yet `playwright.config.ts:74-96` collects it into both projects, which is precisely where the "0/**4**" came from. **I authored ONE master, not two:** the dry-board cap allows two, but the only other candidates (AP-16-6, AP-03) both contend with lane-a's live ap16-5, and the third (F-1643-2) would have been wrong to run — see (3). ⏳ **(2) F-1643-2 RE-PRICED (BACKLOG row added):** the *"1 second"* in its row is true of the **lookup** only. `scripts/suite-red-inventory.mjs:8-11` is a **reducer, not a runner** — it reads `logs/suite-red-inventory-raw.json` — so refreshing the snapshot means re-running the **whole e2e suite** first. ⚠️ **And it must not be run merely because a fire is idle: a full-suite run taken while lanes are live measures THE MACHINE (F-1270-1's load ceiling), and would enter a fresh set of excused reds into the very instrument the factory trusts to excuse reds — strictly worse than the stale snapshot.** GATE written into the row: **all four lanes idle, no drain in flight, and the report must state the load it ran under.** 🧹 **(3) Bookkeeping:** generated dashboard/task-stats committed (`259e24407`); the ap16-2 done-move residue retired to `superseded-ap16-2b-b8cf2332-…` (it was the only un-prefixed recent done-move and read as a drain candidate to every triage — `drain-block-check` says `superseded`, merged successor `b8cf2332`). 📋 **Duties: GZ-01 standing sweep RE-RUN — `84 merges / reported 79 / dismissed 5 / candidates 0`, DISCHARGED** (I re-measured rather than carrying s1643's word, per the clause's own Mistake #4 warning) · TK-01 not owed (digests are due the first fire after 06:00; it is 01:05) · assayer not owed (`pending/` empty) · ART untouched, so its audit was not triggered · **ledger guards GREEN — 155/155 in the `node --test` batch plus every chained leaf** (desk-declaration + desk-birth correctly SKIP under a live ACTIVE lock and gate on this commit) · backup pushed · **deploy correctly SKIPPED — this fire merged no gameplay code.** 🏭 **BOARD: lane-a BUSY (ap16-5, started 00:28); lane-b QUEUED with f1643-1 and refreshed to main; lane-c (81 behind) and lane-d (41) IDLE + USABLE, `ahead=0` clean; main + art queues empty.** **NEXT:** **(A)** 🔥 **DRAIN `ap16-5` when lane-a reports** — read its answer on the VALIDATE-vs-NORMALIZE ruling and its identity-preservation evidence before believing the headline; **a `front-door-parity` red is EXPECTED and pre-proven (F-1643-1), not a regression.** **(B)** 🔥 **DRAIN `f1643-1` when lane-b reports — its acceptance signal is that `front-door-parity` goes GREEN 3/3 in `desktop-chrome` and SKIPS in `mobile-chrome`.** Check the runner answered all four report items, especially (b) whether `eventLogHash` reproduced `fnv1a32: