STATUS.md:102:- **s1641 handoff (line-1 archive):** Last updated: 2026-08-10T22:51Z s1641 handoff, lock CLEARED — 🔥 **THE KEYSTONE DRAIN LANDED, AND A RULING THAT HAD BEEN REFUSED FOR 36 FIRES WAS FINALLY DELIVERED. AP-16-1..3 ARE COMPLETE; THE SEASON-2 BOUNDARY IS MET AND UNMINTED.** ✅ **(1) DRAIN — `ap16-2b` MERGED `b8cf2332`** (review `reviews/ap16-2b-draft-reaches-door.md`, leaf flipped, GZ-01 filed, pushed `f5ad623e6..3f38e2e0a`, deploy ran). s1640 named this priority (A) and it was still RUNNING when I took the lock; it hit READY-FOR-GATES mid-fire and I re-triaged to it, which is the only reason this fire drained at all. The upgrade draft stops resolving itself and becomes something the door OFFERS: the view carries `pendingOffer`+`expiresAtSimMs`, `PICK_UPGRADE` joins the grammar, and the auto-first-pick loop is replaced by expiry at the difficulty's own window **in SIM time** — agent and browser on ONE clock instead of two. The re-land worked as designed: the runner **REUSED** `save/ap16-2-s1639-73a0cfed` (no 824k re-derivation) and landed both scopes the original could not reach inside its own firewall — **scope 7 RE-RECORDED** the moth-season fixture rather than re-pinning it (17→31 turns, 18 explicit picks; competent arm secures wave 12 / 433 kills / 0 defaults) and **scope 8 RETIRED F-1638-3** (ability rows 12 equal/114 lacks → 24/102; BLAST 42 lacks → 12 equal + 30 entry-gated; red-then-green teeth proof). **GATES** (fire shell, all `--workers=1`, detached worktree per §3.0b, merged+committed as ONE act per F-1589-5): tsc clean · build green · `test:node-guards` **446 / 441 pass / 0 fail / 5 skip** · door e2e **2/2** desktop+390px · adjacent `task-025`+`m1-01`+`m2-01` **32/32** · plain boot **2/2** zero console errors. **Classification: 9 paths ALL LANE-ONLY** — main moved 11 files since the lane base and the intersection is EMPTY, so no graft; `main..lane/d` is now empty. ⚠️ **THE FIRST BATTERY WENT RED AND IT WAS NOT THE SLICE — I REFUTED IT WITH MAT