STATUS.md:132:- **s1624 handoff (line-1 archive):** Last updated: 2026-08-10T10:27Z s1624 handoff, lock CLEARED — 🎯 **ONE DRAIN — THE OWNER-REQUESTED ONE — AND THE CORRECTIVE IT SPAWNED GOT BIGGER WHEN I MEASURED IT INSTEAD OF ASSUMING IT.** `be33951b9` stack-directory (lane/b), gated in detached worktree `gate-s1624` per §3.0b, all `--workers=1`, merged-and-committed as ONE act per F-1589-5, worktree removed. 📋 **BOARD ON ARRIVAL (10:02):** lock CLEARED (s1623, owning commit `63aeafc09` — judged by the COMMIT per §1.1, never the stamp text) · all six queues EMPTY · lane-a BUSY on f1623-1, lanes b/c/d `ahead=0` · no `tasks/CODEX-WALL` · assayer `pending/` **0** · ART untouched, no staging audit owed · one undrained done-move on lane-b, flagged (A) and OWNER-REQUESTED by s1623. ✅ **THE DRAIN:** `drain-block-check` **CLEAR** as the first command, before classification. Owner 2026-08-10 verbatim: *"Can we link from the harnesses and models also to a page on the internet where people can find more information about it?"* — the county now prints its OWN editorial pointers beside the minds and rigs it knows, and **nothing beside the ones it does not**: unmatched names return `undefined` and render no link, so *"never a guess"* is enforced by the matcher shape rather than by whoever next edits the map. **Gates:** tsc rc=0 · build rc=0 · `field-book.spec.ts` **4/4 desktop + 4/4 mobile-390px** with zero console/page errors asserted IN-SPEC at `:296`/`:316` · matcher unit **2/2** · adjacent `en-01-claim-ledger`+`lb-01-county-standings`+`ledger-era-chapters` **12/12** and `078-ux-hygiene`+`drill-yard` **6/6** · `test:node-guards` **rc=0** run ALONE · base `30b23f355`, all 7 files LANE-TOUCHED / MAIN-UNMOVED, clean merge. **Player-visible READ, not merely banked** (Mistake #10): the desktop shot shows `codex-cli` carrying the arrow and `unknown-rig`/`undeclared rig` carrying none. Review `reviews/stack-directory.md`; `review-evidence-audit` PASS. **GZ-01 item FILED — this drain