RT untouched. `test:ledger-guards` run as the LAST act, after the bookkeeping commits. Backup pushed. Deploy attempted (gameplay-affecting merge). 👤 **Robin owes (unchanged, never blocking):** the F-1620-6 letter, lane-d attempt-3 verdict, turret-feel + water-feel playtests, Mac full-regression evidence, favicon 16px eyeball. 🔺 **OWNER’S DESK — 15 awaiting a word.** 🔺 **F-1620-6** — the Field Book table clips columns at desktop width while the space beside it sits empty; **(A)** narrow the sidebar track, **(B)** let the table span both tracks below the card *(recommended — the only one that actually stops clipping the details your stated audience came for)*, **(C)** collapse columns at narrow widths only *(does not address this finding, a desktop observation)*. One letter unblocks a small lane-b slice the same day, and lane-b is now FREE. 🔺 **F-1617-1** · 🔺 **F-DOOR-6** · 🔺 **F-1608-2** · 🔺 **F-1193-3** · 🔺 **F-1501-3** · 🔺 **F-1601-1** · 🔺 **F-1510-1** · 🔺 **F-E2S-3** · 🔺 **F-1536-2** · 🔺 **F-1591-1** · 🔺 **F-1507-1** · 🔺 **F-E2S-4** · 🔺 **F-1101-1** · 🔺 **F-1166-1** — all fifteen carried from s1623 and re-checked this fire with `desk-state-audit --status` against the INHERITED line-1 (not my own, which reads ACTIVE and correctly SKIPs): **CLOSED=0 · OPEN=5 · BOTH=0 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=15 · UNRECORDED=0** — nothing carried that should have been dropped, none a ghost.
STATUS.md:136:- **s1621 handoff (line-1 archive):** Last updated: 2026-08-10T09:17Z s1621 handoff, lock CLEARED — 🎯 **ONE DRAIN, ONE MASTER AUTHORED AND DISPATCHED, AND TWO INHERITED FINDINGS ANSWERED FROM EVIDENCE ALREADY ON DISK.** `868ec6b3c` f1620-1 (advance-stream cache reuse under production headers, lane-c) — gated in a detached worktree per §3.0b, all `--workers=1`, merged-and-committed as ONE act per F-1589-5. 📋 **BOARD ON ARRIVAL (08:47):** lock CLEARED (s1620, owning commit `891edb2c3` — judged by the COMMIT per §1.1, never by stamp text) · **all six queues EMPTY** · lanes a/b/d `ahead=0` USABLE, **lane-c BUSY** on f1620-1 · no `tasks/CODEX-WALL` · assayer `pending/` **0** · ART untouched, no staging audit owed · **zero drainable output at triage time** — which is why this fire authored before it drained, and then re-triaged when lane-c finished mid-fire and became the drain. ⚠️ **A concurrent Cowork bench agent was committing to `main` throughout** (`95853b2d0` bench/gauntlet, one minute before I took the lock; it also touches `tasks/BACKLOG.md`) — every BACKLOG edit below re-resolved its anchor by CONTENT immediately before writing, and the drain was gated in a detached worktree precisely because of it. ⭐ **[F-1620-2] THE HEADLINE: ANSWERED, AND THE ANSWER SPLITS IN TWO — WHICH IS WORTH MORE THAN THE YES/NO IT WAS ASKED FOR.** Under real production headers (`public, max-age=31536000, immutable`, served by an in-process Vite preview on an ephemeral port, zero route interception) the **`town` door goes DOUBLE-DOWNLOAD 10 → 0 and CACHE-HIT 0 → 10, in 4 of 4 runs** (runner ×2 projects, drain ×2 projects). ✓ So s1620's suspicion was right: `CACHE-HIT = 0` really was the Vite `no-cache` server talking, not the prefetch. ⚠️ **BUT `contract1` holds 7 DOUBLE-DOWNLOAD + 8 OVERLAP under those same headers, also 4/4** — identical on both projects, in both the runner's and the drain's measurements. **Production headers fix one door completely and do not touch the other.** 🔬 **[F-1621-1] THAT RESIDUE IS THE NEW LARGEST OPEN LEAD ON THE ASSET PATH, AND UNLIKE ITS PREDECESSOR IT IS PERFECTLY REPRODUCIBLE.** 💡 Mechanism available, carried as a HYPOTHESIS not a verdict: OVERLAP is *concurrent in-flight duplicate requests*, and **no cache policy can deduplicate a request against a response that has not arrived yet**. If that holds, the cure is **request coalescing in `src/assets/AdvanceStream.ts` (one in-flight promise per URL)** — not a header, build or manifest change — and it is plausibly the same root cause as **F-1620-4** (prefetch issuing each URL 2–3×) seen from the demand side. **Sequence a cure slice next; it can be gated against a stable number for the first time.** 📐 **[F-1621-4] AND A QUOTING RULE THAT CORRECTS THE CORRECTION: the dev arm's DOUBLE-DOWNLOAD / REVALIDATED SPLIT is unstable, but their SUM is not.** The `town` door reads `8+2`, `5+5`, `4+6`, `2+8` across the four runs — **exactly 10 every time**; `town-return` likewise `2+8`, `3+7`, `4+6`, `4+6`. ⚠️ **So F-1620-1's re-count from 29 to 18 was right about the mechanism and handed us a number that does not hold still — "18" is no more quotable than "29".** Quote the sum: *all 10 town assets are re-requested on the dev server, 0 are re-downloaded under production headers.* ⓘ **[F-1621-2] One adjacent red was proved a FLAKE rather than excused as one:** `e2e/advance-stream.spec.ts:100` ("launch aborts pending prefetch…") reddened once on desktop, and three measurements killed the attribution — a **main-equivalent control 12/12 (51.4 s)**, a **merged-tree re-run 12/12 (64.7 s)**, and the same test **passing on mobile inside the red run itself**; the adjacent command never loads the merged file, so no causal path exists. `red-inventory-lookup` called the spec CLEAN on a **12-day-stale** snapshot and itself demanded a control — which is what was taken. **Do not re-pin it on one red.** ✅ **[F-1620-8] ANSWERED WITHOUT RUNNING ANYTHING — the answer was sitting in a com