rrow check calls 47 ABSENT — 20 are headlined in a ticker, 1 is in the gazette under its short hash, so 21 of 47 are FALSE POSITIVES (44.7%).** ⚠️ **The sentence this refutes is a prior finding’s exoneration:** F-1593-1 audited this very sweep, split it into halves, wrote *“the hash half is a `grep` and cannot go wrong”*, and spent its whole investigation on the other half. **The hash half went wrong in two independent ways, and that exoneration is why nobody looked.** ⓘ The damage is not wasted greps — it is an item that can never be discharged; this one was on its third pass. **Cure is doc-only** in `scripts/fire.md` GZ-01: grep the 8-char SHORT hash across the whole of `marketing/outbox/`. No new guard — the duty’s own prohibition on mechanising this as a red guard is untouched and still right. ✅ **THEN I RAN THE SWEEP PROPERLY AND BACKFILLED WHAT IT FOUND (one ROUNDUP, per the ≤3/week rule).** Of the 47, **4** touch real player source once `e2e/` is dropped (a test is not a player-facing surface), and **3 were genuine misses**: `c8807b4d` (THE FRONT DESK panel beside the county boards — `renderFrontDesk()` + 99 lines of `reader.css`), `7e5fae14` (the e2-trestle terrain rebuild, `Terrain3dClaimPilot.ts` +243), `d9cf6242` (a works with power lines but no connection to make pinned `objectiveAllowsSecure` false forever — **you beat the Baron and it silently failed to secure the claim**). The 4th, `1a2871fd`, is factory hygiene and CORRECTLY absent. 🔎 **A THIRD BLINDNESS, found only by DISCHARGING the duty rather than measuring it — and it is Mistake #16 sitting inside the sweep’s own filter.** s1599 shaped its candidate set by commit-MESSAGE PREFIX (`fix|feat|perf|test|refactor`); **two of my three genuine misses land under subjects naming something else entirely** — `c8807b4d` ships a whole new player-facing panel under *“bench: prime-agent heat 1 closes DNF×3”*, and `7e5fae14` is a bare *“Merge branch ‘lane/c’ into HEAD”*. No amount of widening the sink fixes that