CHANGE MERGE **you drain** … APPEND a news item"* — **the duty was keyed on the AGENT, and the factory's drain load has moved to attended sessions.** Measured, not inferred: four player-visible slices merged attended-side this morning, **all four with review files, all four with ZERO gazette items**, while **all twelve most-recent touches of `gazette-queue.md` are fires at drain time**. Nothing in the pipeline was broken — the trigger simply never fired when a human drained. **BACKFILLED under §7.4** (reversible, additive, ratified pipeline, owner absent): one `## ROUNDUP —` batching the three door/parity merges and one `## GAZETTE —` for f-bal-1 alone, **broken out because it carries a live veto window a roundup would bury**. Two items, not four, on purpose — the ≤3/week rule was already spent (5 items landed 08-07/08-08) and GZ-01 orders the rest batched, so the batching IS the law being obeyed. **RE-KEYED `scripts/fire.md:45` to "ON EVERY REAL-CHANGE MERGE ON MAIN — whoever landed it", with a standing backfill sweep (grep the hash) folded in.** ⓘ **Edited as a single-line REPLACEMENT: `fire.md` is 47 lines before and after, diffed against HEAD — no `law-pointer-guard` coordinate below it rotted.** That check is the duty, not a flourish; this is the surface whose pointers have rotted six times. 🚫 **AND THE CURE DELIBERATELY STOPS SHORT OF A GUARD:** "player-visible" is a judgement, so a red guard on any absent hash fires on every bookkeeping merge and gets excused into uselessness within a week — the `cross-engine` label's exact fate (F-1460-1). A WARN-level list is the most that should ever be built, and it is **explicitly not owed**. 📦 **RETENTION HALF, SIZED AND CLOSED:** the same four attended drains left their cited gate transcripts (`artifacts/{f-door-1,f-door-2,f-bal-1,mp-07b}-gate.txt`, **1.53 MB**) untracked — cited by merged reviews, in no object database, dead with the disk (§10b). Committed; tracking gate transcripts is established convention (`s1481`–