STATUS.md:286:- **s1540 handoff (line-1 archive):** Last updated: 2026-08-08T04:12Z s1540 handoff, lock CLEARED — 🎯 **THE BOARD WAS DRY AGAIN, SO I AUDITED THE 11:00 DISPATCH ITSELF — AND THE RUNNER WILL RUN BOTH BANKED LANE PAIRS BACKWARDS.** 📋 **BOARD ON ARRIVAL:** lock CLEARED (s1539 ended 02:58, judged by its OWNING COMMIT per §1.3) · **six queues EMPTY** · zero undrained done-moves (newest still `drained-51b0bc35c`) · `tasks/failed/` all old labelled dispositions · assayer `pending/` EMPTY · **NO DRAIN EXISTED.** Ref sweep run BEFORE accepting the dry verdict: lanes a/b/c/d all `ahead=0`, all 8 `milk/*` `ahead=0`; `lane/m3`+`lane/m4` read 5/7 ahead but are the retired permanently-ahead branches, not undrained work. ⛔ **CODEX-WALL ACTIVE until 11:00 — no refills, and I did NOT run §2.0’s probe**, same reason as s1538/s1539: the wall is OWNER-WORDED with a fixed lift time, not the rolling-window kind a probe retires early. 👤 **ATTENDED QUIET** since 02:15; the 4 dirty files (`artifacts/agent-seat/*`, 3 generated `logs/*`) are the same regeneration churn s1538 and s1539 both declined to bank, and **I declined it too**. 🔎 **F-1540-1 — THE RUNNER DISPATCHES ALPHABETICALLY, AND BOTH BANKED PAIRS SORT WRONG.** `lane-runner-v3.sh:68` is `f=$(ls "$q"/*.md | head -1)` — plain alphabetical, no sequencing input. The MP-07 ladder says **mp-07a before f-door-1** (lane-b) and **mp-07b before f-e2s-1** (lane-d), but `lane-fdoor1-*` and `lane-fe2s1-*` both sort BEFORE `lane-mp07a-*`/`lane-mp07b-*` — so a fire that copies both masters of a pair into one queue at 11:00 runs the ladder in **reverse**, and both written “after X” clauses become silently void. ✅ **NO DATA LOSS, which is the half worth knowing:** the F-1522-1 pre-dispatch guard refuses the second dispatch once the first commits (HOLDS → `REFUSE`, queue file stays queued, **zero Codex tokens**). I did not take that on trust — `lane-dispatch-safety-guard.test.sh` ran **8/8 GREEN** this fire, incl. `REFUSES-HOLDS`, `DISPATCHES-DIRTY-RC2` and `DISPATCHES-PROBE-FAIL-OPEN` (the last two document deliberate fail-open paths). So 2-deep lane queues are **SAFE but ORDER-BLIND**. ⓘ Harmless *this time* only because the attended session authored defensively — both second masters carry explicit order-tolerant SEQUENCING (f-e2s-1: *“No other dependency; if the file matches main, proceed on main”*; f-door-1: *“none on other tasks”*). **A latent trap defused by care, not by mechanism.** ➡️ **CURE IS OPERATIONAL AND FREE, AND I WROTE IT INTO THE LADDER ITSELF** (not just the finding row, so the 11:00 fire meets it where it looks): copy **ONE master per lane** — `mp-07a`→lane-b, `mp-07b`→lane-d — and add f-door-1/f-e2s-1 only after their predecessors DRAIN. ⚠️ **AND IT CORRECTS s1539, whose cure I re-verified as CORRECT AND NECESSARY on its primary claim.** s1539’s secondary rationale — *“AND IT COMPOUNDS: whichever ran second would `-B` force-reset it back to main over the first’s undrained output — the Reset Massacre shape”* — is **REFUTED by reading the resolver**: `lane-usable.mjs` `fleet()` keys on the worktree **PATH** and reports whatever branch that worktree currently sits on, so it would have FOLLOWED lane-d onto `lane/perf` and refused the dispatch. I also closed a worry of my own rather than banking it: `lane/perf` is **`0` ahead of main**, so the `-B` would have destroyed no retired history either. **The vanished-casualty half of F-1539-1 stands and its cure was necessary; only the compounding clause was wrong.** 🔎 **F-1540-2 — A STALE MAPPING SURVIVED ITS OWN CURE, PROTECTED BY A NOTE SAYING IT HADN’T (FIXED `31199d142`).** `scripts/lane-usable.mjs:76-77` still asserted *“lane-a is lane/m3 … lane-d is **lane/perf**”* — the mapping F-1464-3 measured FALSE and corrected in `fire.md`/`CLAUDE.md`. ⚠️ **The compounding part:** `scripts/lane-branches.sh:25-26` (s1536) recorded that the F-1464-3 cure *“reached the prose **and lane-usable.mjs**”* — **verified FALSE**: no commit after `eef64e