waiting a word.** 🔺 **F-1499-2 OPEN (the big one, gates the whole ER-03 wave): DOES A HEADLESS RIDER GET A BODY?** Either the headless sim grows a movement/progression path and the E2 maps are playable as drawn, or GR-SIM contracts are declared **works-only puzzles** and E2 is balanced for a stationary hero. Narrowed by F-1528-3: the Prospector already HAS a moving body headlessly, so the question is about the **HERO**. F-ER02-5/6 wait on it. 🔺 **F-1529-4 NEW — `claim_damage`, the second storm trigger (7.75× protocol cost for 0 extra waves on `e2-incline`), needs a pick between a RATE-LIMIT and a WINDOW.** Unlike `order_failure` it has **no status/reason pair to de-dupe against**, so there is no invariant to restore and a fire may not choose. **RECOMMENDATION: a window** — it degrades gracefully under a damage burst, where a rate-limit silently drops the tail. 🔺 **F-1101-1 / `calibrate-suite-workers-v2` OPEN — RECOMMENDATION: RETIRE THE THREAD.** The correctness half is shipped and guarded; only the lane-shell optimisation is uncalibrated and nobody has felt it. 🔺 **F-1166-1 / `vp-02e-jumper-8way-activation` OPEN — owner picks (a) ACCEPT COARSE (recommended) or (b) FINISH THE JUMPER (an ART batch + a src/ slice; it spends money).** 🔺 **`rf-34-hero-y-restore-roundtrip` OPEN** (the reserved fork s1104 merged and had to reverse). 🔺 **`e3-fairground-socket` OPEN.** 🔺 **`bt-04-homestead-automation` OPEN.** 🔺 **`f1328-1-drill-yard-census-debt` OPEN (`blockClass: disputed`):** its reserved question is measured **vacuous as stated** and scope item 1 is dispatched elsewhere; what remains is a judgement — *does a byte-stable fixture of a wrong derivation bless it or catch it?*
