ression path and the E2 maps are playable as drawn, or GR-SIM contracts are declared **works-only puzzles** and E2 is balanced for a stationary hero. **NEW EVIDENCE THIS FIRE (F-1528-3): the Prospector already HAS a moving body headlessly — measured, four distinct positions in four turns — so the question is narrower than it reads: it is about the HERO.** F-ER02-5/6 wait on it; the three protocol repairs did not, and all three have now landed. 🔺 **F-1101-1 / `calibrate-suite-workers-v2` OPEN — RECOMMENDATION: RETIRE THE THREAD.** The correctness half is shipped and guarded; only the lane-shell optimisation is uncalibrated and nobody has felt it. 🔺 **F-1166-1 / `vp-02e-jumper-8way-activation` OPEN — owner picks (a) ACCEPT COARSE (recommended) or (b) FINISH THE JUMPER (an ART batch + a src/ slice; it spends money).** 🔺 **`rf-34-hero-y-restore-roundtrip` OPEN** (the reserved fork s1104 merged and had to reverse). 🔺 **`e3-fairground-socket` OPEN.** 🔺 **`bt-04-homestead-automation` OPEN.** 🔺 **`f1328-1-drill-yard-census-debt` OPEN (`blockClass: disputed`):** its reserved question is measured **vacuous as stated** and scope item 1 is dispatched elsewhere; what remains is a judgement — *does a byte-stable fixture of a wrong derivation bless it or catch it?*
