ers matched, not merely counts.** 🎨 **AUTHORED *AND* RAN f1608-1 IN ONE FIRE — AND ITS FAILURE IS THE DELIVERABLE.** F-1193-3 had waited ~400 fires for the owner\'s fourth premise (*"Spend one more batch"* → standalone single-row sheets, composited). The ART runner claimed the slot inside a minute and **STOPPED LAWFULLY**: container 1983×793 (`1983 % 4 = 3`), coal sack **R,R,R,R** where **L,L,L,L** was required, key impure (70 of 1,572,519 px exact). **The master ordered a stop rather than a fifth premise and the runner obeyed exactly — Steam Wrecker never generated, no shipped pixel changed, 8/8 rows byte-identical.** ⭐ **Three prior premises varied the WORDING; this varied the CONTAINER, so the container is now REFUTED** — the one thing three attempts never established. 🧭 **TWO AUTHORING TRAPS FOUND AND DISARMED BEFORE DISPATCH:** the predecessor master\'s pre-flight demands the sheets be *"the shipped originals"*, now **FALSE for Steam Wrecker** (two commits — the s1193 PARTIAL legitimately landed row 2), so a runner obeying it would **STOP on a healthy tree**; and its scope item 1 (the `cast.json` prop fix) **already landed**, so it is firewalled OFF. 📚 **F-1536-2 CENSUS TAKEN (one of F-1601-1\'s nine, one per fire): 67 `save/*` refs → 54 ABSORBED · 13 HOLDS · 0 DEAD**, via `scripts/salvage-census.mjs` asking the one-directional `main..ref` question. **The deferral\'s own premise is refuted** — a dynamic panel would show **13**, not 66, and filtering on absorbed-ness rather than the `save/`-vs-`archive/` NAME reads correctly whether or not the renames ever happen. Rename blast radius measured **ZERO**. I did **not** rename or edit the panel: the row reserves both, and a specific reservation outranks my general reading of §7.4. 📮 **GZ-01 SWEEP RE-PRICED AND RUN (F-1608-1):** `scripts/gazette-backfill-sweep.mjs` greps the **whole outbox**, indexes citations **by prefix** (an 8-char slice cannot match a 7-char citation), and tests **contained commits** too. **68 merges · 60 cited · 8 candidates → 3 owed, 1 already reported, 4 not player-visible.** Wrote **1 GAZETTE + 1 ROUNDUP**; fort-solidity broke out **separately because it carries a LIVE OWNER CHOICE** (may landmark forts ever be damaged or besieged — the wrecker waits on the same word), which the law says a roundup must never bury. 🔑 **NEW BLIND SPOT FOUND: a feature landing across TWO merges and announced ONCE leaves the first merge permanently "absent"** — `ba78dad5e` reads unreported but the county-board item published its outcome under the later `964978bad`. The duty is to report a CHANGE; the check is keyed on HASHES. ⚠️ **F-1608-3 — A STRAY GITLINK, CAUGHT AND REMOVED.** While I gated in a detached worktree exactly as §3.0b orders, the ART runner\'s broad `git add` swept **`gate-s1608` into main as `160000 74bd3424…`** — a submodule-shaped pointer at a path that no longer exists, i.e. garbage in every future clone, surviving review as one boring line in a 20-file art commit. **The collision is STRUCTURAL:** §3.0b says gate in a detached worktree, the permission gate requires it **inside the repo root**, and the ART slot is the one writer still using a broad add. **REC (next fire, one line): add `gate-*/` to `.gitignore` and confirm a broad add skips it.** 🔭 **NEXT FIRE (A)** — **`gate-*/` in `.gitignore`** (F-1608-3), the cheapest real act on the board. **(B)** the **TK-01 daily digest for 2026-08-09**, owed by the first fire after 06:00 local — **not owed by me at 01:50**. **(C)** F-1536-2\'s 54 renames + dynamic panel: **one word unlocks a 30-second job**, all uncertainty removed. **(D)** F-1601-1\'s remaining eight work-acts, one per fire. ⓘ Two things I left alone deliberately: the artifact/log churn in main\'s tree (a live `codex review --uncommitted` was reading it — the ART commit swept it anyway, harmlessly), and the **582 files / 527.89 MB** ART staging hole, which is **already filed as F-1501-3** and is an owner call because the cure is half a gigabyte of