   139	# e1-baron attempt — prime-r1
   140	
   141	## Pre-run hypothesis
   142	
   143	The prior best treated palisades as a long blocking wall and spent its boss reserve repairing remote wrecks while too few guns could reach the Baron. I will instead finish the actual damage engine before wave 20: three income sluices, all four turrets at tier III in a tight north-bank kill box, six nearby beacons, and an offense-weighted thirty-pick draft. At wave 19 I will add separated 10-gold palisades as disposable rocket/strike decoys, with only the first narrow center panel intercepting the ford. Its wave-scaled HP should fall just below 31% after a 128-damage Baron strike, so `REPAIR_UNDER 31` deterministically selects it without paying for ordinary scratches. Between damage/repair observations, brief `blast`→`rig` standing-order pairs should fire an auto-aimed Blast Charge while keeping the Spark Rig active; an explicit cooldown refusal creates the next deterministic observation.
   144	
   145	This differs from the failed line-and-stockpile plan by concentrating every capped gun inside the boss stop point, maxing turret tiers before luxury economy, and using cheap, separated shot decoys rather than a remote fortification line.
   146	
   147	## Result
   148	
   149	_Pending run._
   150	
   151	--- r2-codex-6-sol.md ---
   152	# e1-baron attempt — codex-6-sol-r2
   153	
   154	## Hypothesis
   155	
   156	The failed palisade-wall runs spent their reserve repairing remote wrecks while too few weapons could reach the Baron. I will instead compound three sluices into four T3 turrets in a tight north-bank kill box, add six nearby beacons, and place three wave-19 palisades as disposable shot decoys rather than a long wall. Only the center decoy at `(0, 11)` will be eligible for a narrow repair policy. An offense-heavy draft plus repeated `blast` → `rig` cycling and directed blasts at the stop should supply enough damage while preserving sustained rig fire.
   157	
   158	This follows the reference tape's principle—upgrade a small damage engine and actively switch weapons—while avoiding the failed campaign's spread-out wall and generic late repair drain.
   159	
   160	## Result — SECURED
   161	
   162	```json
   163	{"secured":true,"waves":22,"timeMs":596967,"gold":319,"kills":985,"calls":3294,"defaultedPicks":0,"defaultedSecure":0,"eventLogHash":"fnv1a32:f5365f4c"}
   164	```
   165	
   166	The first run secured at wave 22, so I stopped within the six-run limit.
   167	
   168	## What I did
   169	
   170	- Built three sluices, six sentry beacons, four turrets, and two stockpiles; all sluices and turrets reached T3 before the boss fight.
   171	- Concentrated the turret line at z=12 and added the center palisade `(0, 11)` plus disposable side decoys `(-10, 11)` and `(10, 11)` at wave 19.
   172	- Prioritized Heavy Spark, Split Spark, Double Tap, Long Resonator, Powder Charge, Quick Fuse, and Beacon Dynamo, with Tinker's Plating for late survivability.
   173	- During the boss fight, cycled `SET_WEAPON blast` → `SET_WEAPON rig`, aimed `BLAST_AT` at `(0, 11)`, held at `(0, 12)`, and allowed only the center palisade to trigger `REPAIR_UNDER 31`.
   174	- Explicitly banked the secure choice; no upgrade or secure choice defaulted.
   175	
   176	## Why it won
   177	
   178	The upgraded sluices paid for the complete T3 turret engine early enough that the defense entered the Baron fight with real concentrated damage. The late palisades had 172 HP each: the side panels absorbed attacks and were allowed to die, while the center blocker was restored and kept the Baron at the gun line. The final combat view had the Prospector at 167/175 HP, the center palisade at 172/172, both side decoys wrecked, and three T3 turrets still firing. The run ended with 319 gold, so selective repair avoided the reserve exhaustion seen in the failed wall strategies.
   179	
   180	## Source-grounded note for the next rig
   181	
   182	`src/entities/Enemy.ts:953-959` makes the Baron prefer a palisade that blocks his route to the hero, while `src/systems/BuildSystem.ts:1957-1965` gives a late-placed palisade wave-scaled HP. Keep the center decoy first in palisade index order: `src/agent/StandingOrders.ts:268-276` selects the first building below the repair threshold, so a narrow `REPAIR_UNDER 31` can restore that blocker without funding ordinary damage elsewhere. `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:243-269` also defines separate rig and Blast shooters, which is why brief Blast-to-rig cycles can layer a Blast shot over continuous rig fire.
