# Baron props replace the wrecker stone with a powder keg

F-BW-18 gives the [[Gold Rush MOC|Gold Rush]] Baron's carried launcher and volley projectiles one deterministic detail pack: a 2,020-triangle timber-and-brass three-rocket rack, an 876-triangle banded flight rocket, and a 704-triangle iron-banded powder keg. The pack uses one 512 atlas and one material; reopening the saved Blender source and re-exporting produces a byte-identical GLB.

The owner's “stone” was the shared wrecker carry marker, not a projectile. `createClaimJumperAssets().sackGeometry` is a 0.23-radius, detail-0 dodecahedron. Because the Baron is a wrecker, the generic marker appeared beside his sprite as a brown low-poly stone. The Baron alone now suppresses that marker and carries the dedicated powder keg; other wreckers are unchanged.

The existing volley simulation remains authoritative. Baron shots now layer a pooled detailed rocket and short ash/ember puffs over the same CombatSystem lob, while the Baron's generic teal dodecahedron and full-path wire are hidden. Targeting, cadence, damage, air time, impacts, and the settled Baron sprite are unchanged. This continues [[Baron fight uses rendered bar telemetry and a carried launcher — 2026-07-13 0755]] and stays separate from [[Baron siege targets the blocking palisade — 2026-08-03 1812]].

Fresh visual review passed on desktop and 390 px mobile. Mid-volley p95 was 10.3 → 10.3 ms desktop and 9.8 → 9.9 ms mobile, both within the +15% ceiling. Release batteries passed. The Baron suite is 20/22 only because its existing board-census assertion still expects five E1 cards while the current roster has six after Drill Yard; the task did not edit that out-of-scope existing e2e spec.

Evidence and full gate detail are in `artifacts/baron-props/report.md` in the lane-d worktree.

